{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Land worth four hundred shekels of silver.</b> As its Targum renders: land that is worth thus much. Or one may say that Ephron, or his ancient ancestors, had acquired it for this sum. And the view of our Rabbis, of blessed memory, is that it was not worth so much, but Ephron set the price at a great premium, and Abraham, out of his generosity, agreed to the matter." "<b>And by way of the Midrash.</b> ״Land of four hundred shekels of silver, what is it between me and you?״ — the righteous say little and do much. Whence? From Abraham, who said (Genesis 18:5) ״ואקחה פת לחם״, and it is written ״מהרי שלש סאים קמח סלת״, and it is written ״ואל הבקר רץ אברהם״. But the wicked say much and do not do even a little. Whence? From Ephron, who said to Abraham ״ארץ ארבע מאות שקל כסף וגו׳״, and in the end it is written ״וישקול אברהם לעפרון״ — עבר לסחר. Ephron was wicked and narrow-eyed: עפרן is written חסר (defective), in gematria ר״ע עי״ן." "<b>And see:</b> Abraham was one who hated gifts and did not wish to accept a gift from him but only for full silver, and such is the way of the righteous. And so we find with King David, peace be upon him, that he purchased the threshing floor and did not wish to accept it from Araunah, who was giving it to him as a gift. And this is what is written (II Samuel 24:22): ״ויאמר ארונה אל דוד יקח ויעל אדני המלך הטוב בעיניו ראה הבקר לעולה והמוריגים וכלי הבקר לעצים״. And David answered him: No, for I shall surely purchase it from you for a price, and I shall not offer up to HaShem burnt-offerings gratis — and it is written: ״ויקן דוד את הגרן ואת הבקר בכסף שקלים חמשים ויבן שם דוד מזבח לה׳״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {1 "The phrase 'עבר לסחר' appears to be a running-on of the next verse's words 'עובר לסוחר' (Genesis 23:16) into the comment text; the MT reads עובר (with vav). The gematria note plays on the defective spelling עפרן (without the letter vav) equalling the numerical value of רע עין."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:14:31.983943314Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}